WEBVTT

00:08.755 --> 00:12.254
(water trickling, dripping)

00:23.421 --> 00:25.338
(dosimeter clicking)

00:25.421 --> 00:28.755
(muffled labored breathing)

00:32.463 --> 00:36.171
(flashlight whirring)

00:38.338 --> 00:40.963
(whirring)

00:45.838 --> 00:48.046
(whirring)

00:50.755 --> 00:53.713
-(dosimeters clicking)
-(man grunting)

01:02.713 --> 01:05.463
(muffled voices)

01:07.129 --> 01:09.213
(water sloshing)

01:23.254 --> 01:25.672
(muffled grunts)

02:11.046 --> 02:12.797
(sighs)

02:12.880 --> 02:15.963
Is it possible that the water
has already killed them?

02:16.046 --> 02:18.296
Yes.

02:18.380 --> 02:20.046
Then what?

02:21.213 --> 02:23.088
If it doesn't work?

02:24.755 --> 02:27.713
(distant helicopters whopping)

02:40.672 --> 02:43.421
(dosimeters clicking loudly)

02:46.380 --> 02:48.421
(flashlights whirring)

02:54.797 --> 02:57.421
(muffled grunts)

03:11.296 --> 03:13.463
(dosimeters clicking loudly)

03:28.963 --> 03:31.296
(banging on door)

03:35.630 --> 03:38.421
(panting, grunting)

03:38.505 --> 03:39.755
(gasping)

03:39.838 --> 03:42.171
(soldiers applauding)

03:42.254 --> 03:44.963
(indistinct cheering)

03:55.797 --> 03:58.046
Get them
in the truck.

03:58.129 --> 04:00.463
Get the hoses in!
Start pumping!

04:16.672 --> 04:19.421
Uh, I'm here
to see my husband,
Vasily Ignatenko.

04:19.505 --> 04:22.254
He's a firefighter
from Chernobyl.
I have permission.

04:22.338 --> 04:25.213
Chernobyl?
I'm sorry, no visitors.

04:27.213 --> 04:29.588
Well, but Major Burov told me,

04:29.672 --> 04:31.046
-he said--
-No exceptions.

04:31.129 --> 04:33.880
Please. I've come all the way
from Kievskaya Oblast.

04:59.755 --> 05:01.546
Excuse me.

05:02.963 --> 05:04.129
Excuse me, excuse me.

05:04.213 --> 05:05.922
Who are you?
What are you doing here?

05:06.004 --> 05:08.630
-I have a pass.
-You can't be here.
It's not safe.

05:08.713 --> 05:10.296
I am here to see
my husband.

05:10.380 --> 05:11.630
Vasily Ignatenko.

05:11.713 --> 05:13.296
He's a firefighter
from Chernobyl.

05:13.380 --> 05:15.963
I know who Ignatenko is,
but you can't.

05:16.046 --> 05:18.088
I have permission.
I-I've...

05:24.380 --> 05:27.296
You can see him
for 30 minutes,
not a minute more.

05:27.380 --> 05:30.630
And you cannot touch
him in any way.
Do you understand?

05:30.713 --> 05:32.546
-Yeah.
-Room 15.

05:34.797 --> 05:36.213
Thank you.

05:36.296 --> 05:38.213
-You're not pregnant,
are you?
-No.

05:46.004 --> 05:47.755
I won't have to give
that to you.

05:47.838 --> 05:49.088
There they are.

05:49.171 --> 05:51.004
No, wait, wait, wait.
I haven't finished yet.

05:51.088 --> 05:52.380
No, he hasn't.

05:52.463 --> 05:54.338
Yeah, that's good.

05:57.380 --> 05:58.755
Yeah, better.

06:01.421 --> 06:03.254
Look who the cat
dragged in.

06:05.088 --> 06:07.088
What did I tell you?

06:08.129 --> 06:10.963
-There's no hiding
from you, is there?
-(both laughing)

06:12.004 --> 06:13.046
(groans)

06:13.129 --> 06:15.755
Easy, easy. It's okay.

06:15.838 --> 06:19.171
We're all okay.
Yeah, we're okay.

06:25.046 --> 06:28.922
(distant wind howling)

06:29.004 --> 06:32.546
(distant dosimeter clicking)

06:39.296 --> 06:42.546
(helicopter whomping)

06:42.630 --> 06:44.797
(indistinct voices)

06:49.296 --> 06:51.380
(dosimeter clicking)

06:58.088 --> 07:01.296
(clicking grows louder)

07:29.171 --> 07:32.630
How, how, how did this happen?
Who gave them the idea?

07:32.713 --> 07:34.588
-Are you suggesting I did?
-Someone did.

07:34.672 --> 07:38.129
Someone decided
that the evacuation zone

07:38.213 --> 07:41.421
should be 30 kilometers,
when we know, here,

07:41.505 --> 07:44.171
Cesium-137
in the Gomel district.

07:44.254 --> 07:46.630
-That's 200 kilometers away!
-It was decided.

07:46.713 --> 07:49.213
-Based on what?
-I don't know!

07:50.380 --> 07:54.463
Forgive me. Maybe I've just
spent too much time in my lab.

07:54.546 --> 07:56.296
Or maybe I'm just stupid.

07:56.380 --> 07:59.588
Is this really the way
it all works?

07:59.672 --> 08:01.588
An uninformed,
arbitrary decision

08:01.672 --> 08:03.922
that will cost who knows
how many lives

08:04.004 --> 08:07.963
made by some apparatchik,
some career party man?

08:10.213 --> 08:12.421
I'm a career party man.

08:13.046 --> 08:16.088
You should watch your tone,
Comrade Legasov.

08:17.380 --> 08:19.129
Pikalov:
Comrades...

08:19.213 --> 08:21.797
We have visual confirmation
that the fire is nearly
extinguished.

08:21.880 --> 08:24.088
There has also been
a reduction in iodine 131

08:24.171 --> 08:26.171
and cesium-137 emissions.

08:26.254 --> 08:28.171
Good. Yes?

08:28.254 --> 08:31.171
Pikalov:
But the temperature
is rising.

08:31.254 --> 08:32.755
And, uh...

08:39.797 --> 08:42.922
There's a spike
in zirconium-95.

08:44.088 --> 08:47.380
It's from the cladding
on the fuel rods.

08:47.463 --> 08:49.838
Meaning what?

08:49.922 --> 08:52.463
The meltdown has begun.

08:55.797 --> 08:57.922
(helicopters whomping)

09:03.129 --> 09:05.254
(water drops plunking)

09:22.129 --> 09:24.213
(distant man moans)

09:25.630 --> 09:28.672
(moaning continues)

09:30.880 --> 09:32.546
Man:
Get it off me!

09:35.046 --> 09:37.505
Get it off me!

09:39.380 --> 09:42.630
(man wailing)

09:44.588 --> 09:46.380
Nurse:
Stop moving!

09:46.463 --> 09:49.129
-Get off him!
You're hurting him!
-(Vasily wailing)

09:49.213 --> 09:52.004
-You can't be in here.
-What's happening to him?

09:52.088 --> 09:54.254
-Get out!
-(Vasily screaming)

09:54.338 --> 09:56.338
You can't be in here!

10:00.380 --> 10:03.338
-(door slams)
-(muffled screaming)

10:33.672 --> 10:35.546
(papers rustle)

10:36.088 --> 10:37.380
(phone rings)

10:39.129 --> 10:41.254
-Yes?
-Man (over phone):
Comrade Shcherbina is
on the phone.

10:41.338 --> 10:42.755
Put him through.

10:44.213 --> 10:45.380
Well?

10:45.463 --> 10:47.088
Shcherbina:
The fire's nearly out.

10:47.171 --> 10:48.838
The bubbler tanks
are being drained.

10:48.922 --> 10:52.046
We have successfully eliminated
the risk of a thermal explosion.

10:52.129 --> 10:54.088
(sighs)

10:55.254 --> 10:56.296
And?

10:57.797 --> 10:59.296
The situation inside the core

10:59.380 --> 11:02.171
is deteriorating
faster than anticipated.

11:02.254 --> 11:05.129
The concrete pad will last
for six to eight weeks,

11:05.213 --> 11:08.421
but after that,
Legasov estimates a 50% chance

11:08.505 --> 11:10.588
that the fuel will
breach the pad

11:10.672 --> 11:13.088
and melt down into
the groundwater itself.

11:13.171 --> 11:16.463
(stammers)
And where does this
groundwater go?

11:16.546 --> 11:18.505
The Pripyat River,

11:18.588 --> 11:21.505
which feeds into the Dnieper.

11:21.588 --> 11:25.129
The primary water supply for
approximately 50 million people,

11:25.213 --> 11:26.963
not to mention crops
and livestock,

11:27.046 --> 11:29.088
would be... unusable.

11:29.171 --> 11:32.046
We're recommending we install
a heat exchanger under the pad

11:32.129 --> 11:35.129
to lower to core temperature
and halt the meltdown.

11:35.213 --> 11:39.296
And in order to do that,
I'm told that we will need...

11:40.755 --> 11:44.797
all of the liquid nitrogen
in the Soviet Union.

11:46.713 --> 11:47.922
Gorbachev:
Oh.

11:49.213 --> 11:51.630
- All right.
-Yeah, and of course,
we'll also need--

11:51.713 --> 11:53.254
Whatever you need,
you have it.

11:53.338 --> 11:54.755
- That should be
clear by now.
-Yes.

11:54.838 --> 11:56.380
- Anything else?
-No, no, no. Thank you.

11:56.463 --> 11:59.380
Yes. I'd like to address
the 30-kilometer
exclusion zone.

11:59.463 --> 12:02.546
Wait, what?
Professor Legasov,
is that you?

12:02.630 --> 12:03.630
What exclusion zone?

12:03.713 --> 12:05.797
Minor details,
General Secretary.

12:05.880 --> 12:08.380
Um, Premier Ryzhkov
has determined that--

12:08.463 --> 12:10.546
If he determined,
then he determined.

12:10.630 --> 12:12.296
Look, Professor Legasov,

12:12.380 --> 12:14.380
you    are there
for one reason only.

12:14.463 --> 12:16.546
Do you understand?
To make this stop.

12:16.630 --> 12:17.922
I don't want questions.

12:18.004 --> 12:19.713
I want to know when
this will be over.

12:19.797 --> 12:21.963
If you mean when will
Chernobyl be completely safe,

12:22.046 --> 12:25.171
the half-life of plutonium-239
is 24,000 years.

12:25.254 --> 12:28.463
So perhaps we should just say,
"Not within our lifetimes."

12:30.254 --> 12:31.838
(line clicks)

12:40.797 --> 12:42.713
I think you and I
should take a walk.

12:42.797 --> 12:44.838
It's late. I'm tired.

12:45.838 --> 12:48.380
We're taking a walk.

12:50.171 --> 12:52.338
(dog panting)

12:54.838 --> 12:57.421
Was it it you want?
An apology?

12:58.797 --> 13:00.463
Not gonna sit back and...

13:00.546 --> 13:02.546
-(dog whining)
-(Legasov sighs)

13:02.630 --> 13:05.588
What will happen
to our boys?

13:05.672 --> 13:07.963
Which boys?
The divers?

13:08.046 --> 13:11.380
The divers, the firefighters,
the men in the control room.

13:11.463 --> 13:15.046
What does the radiation
do to them precisely?

13:16.672 --> 13:19.380
At the levels some
of them were exposed?

13:19.463 --> 13:23.296
Ionizing radiation tears
the cellular structure apart.

13:23.380 --> 13:26.963
The skin blisters,
turns red, then black.

13:28.088 --> 13:30.797
This is followed
by a latency period.

13:31.880 --> 13:33.672
The immediate
effects subside.

13:33.755 --> 13:36.797
The patient appears
to be recovering.

13:36.880 --> 13:39.296
Healthy, even.
But they aren't.

13:40.880 --> 13:44.421
This usually only lasts
for a day or two.

13:46.797 --> 13:48.088
Continue.

13:49.254 --> 13:52.963
Then the cellular damage
begins to manifest.

13:53.046 --> 13:58.380
The bone marrow dies,
the immune system fails,

13:58.463 --> 14:02.254
the organs and soft tissue
begin to decompose.

14:02.338 --> 14:06.338
The arteries and veins
spill open like sieves,

14:06.421 --> 14:08.880
to the point where you can't
even administer morphine

14:08.963 --> 14:13.213
for the pain,
which is... unimaginable.

14:13.296 --> 14:16.797
And then three days
to three weeks, you are dead.

14:19.046 --> 14:21.463
That is what will happen
to those boys.

14:23.588 --> 14:25.088
And what about us?

14:28.338 --> 14:30.004
Well, we've...

14:30.088 --> 14:34.254
We've gotten a steady dose,
but not as much of it.

14:34.338 --> 14:36.338
Not strong enough
to kill the cells,

14:36.421 --> 14:39.463
but consistent enough
to damage our DNA.

14:40.963 --> 14:44.213
So, in time... cancer.

14:44.296 --> 14:47.505
Or aplastic anemia.
Either way, fatal.

14:50.463 --> 14:51.838
Well...

14:53.421 --> 14:59.338
in a sense, it would seem we've
gotten off easy then, Valery.

15:11.880 --> 15:13.880
I've seen them before.

15:19.630 --> 15:22.880
Now you know why
I wanted to take a walk.

15:23.004 --> 15:25.505
We can presume
the work site is bugged.

15:26.171 --> 15:30.088
And our rooms,
even our bathrooms.

15:30.171 --> 15:32.588
They've been here
the whole time.

15:32.672 --> 15:34.755
Of course they've been
here the whole time.

15:36.004 --> 15:39.588
But if we're seeing them
out in the open now,

15:39.672 --> 15:42.505
it's because
they want us to know.

15:49.421 --> 15:52.171
(distant helicopters thrumming)

15:59.421 --> 16:02.672
(door opens, closes)

16:24.296 --> 16:25.755
Khomyuk:
You've seen that?

16:28.004 --> 16:30.129
The fuel is melting
faster than we expected.

16:30.213 --> 16:33.254
I know. I have a plan.

16:33.338 --> 16:35.963
Heat exchanger, I hope.

16:36.046 --> 16:37.546
Yes.

16:40.463 --> 16:42.463
There's something I've wanted
to ask you, comrade,

16:42.546 --> 16:45.963
but I see you're already asking
yourself the same question.

16:49.963 --> 16:52.338
Why did it explode?

16:53.838 --> 16:56.046
I've worked the numbers
over and over,

16:56.129 --> 17:00.004
presuming the worst possible
conditions in an RBMK reactor.

17:01.755 --> 17:04.338
And I always get
the same answer.

17:04.421 --> 17:05.922
Which is?

17:07.254 --> 17:09.505
It's not possible.

17:09.588 --> 17:11.088
And yet...

17:14.171 --> 17:16.421
You're not going
to solve this here.

17:17.963 --> 17:19.588
Not on paper.

17:21.088 --> 17:22.963
Everyone who was
in the control room,

17:23.046 --> 17:25.338
Dyatlov, Akimov, Toptunov,

17:25.421 --> 17:29.588
they're all in Moscow,
Hospital Number 6.

17:29.672 --> 17:32.880
We need to find out exactly
what happened that night,

17:32.963 --> 17:36.505
moment by moment,
decision by decision.

17:37.713 --> 17:40.004
Go now while
they're still alive.

17:40.088 --> 17:41.963
Talk to them.

17:42.046 --> 17:44.922
Because if we don't find out
how this happened,

17:45.004 --> 17:47.338
it will happen again.

17:50.254 --> 17:52.046
And, Khomyuk...

17:53.505 --> 17:55.838
be careful.

18:02.004 --> 18:03.546
(elevator dings)

18:06.463 --> 18:08.505
(trucks rumbling)

18:19.672 --> 18:21.046
Well, fuck you!

18:21.129 --> 18:24.088
(men laughing)

18:24.171 --> 18:26.171
Hey, here's one, here's one.

18:26.254 --> 18:28.171
What's as big as a house,

18:28.254 --> 18:31.129
burns 20 liters
of fuel every hour,

18:31.213 --> 18:33.088
puts out a shit-load
of smoke and noise,

18:33.171 --> 18:37.088
and cuts an apple
into three pieces?

18:39.129 --> 18:42.546
A Soviet machine made to cut
apples into four pieces!

18:42.630 --> 18:44.922
(men laughing)

18:49.129 --> 18:51.254
(men laughing)

19:21.880 --> 19:25.046
-Who's in charge here?
-Glukhov: I'm the crew chief.

19:25.129 --> 19:29.129
I am Shadov,
minister of coal industries.

19:29.213 --> 19:30.880
We know who you are.

19:33.004 --> 19:34.505
How many men do you have?

19:34.588 --> 19:38.713
On this shift, 45 here,
a hundred in total.

19:38.797 --> 19:43.171
I need all 100 men
to gather their equipment
and get in the trucks.

19:43.254 --> 19:46.755
Do you? To where?

19:48.254 --> 19:49.588
That's classified.

19:55.922 --> 19:57.088
Come on, then.

19:57.171 --> 19:58.797
Start shooting.

19:58.880 --> 20:02.088
You haven't got enough
bullets for all of us.

20:02.171 --> 20:04.171
Kill as many as you can,
whoever's left,

20:04.254 --> 20:06.088
they'll beat the living piss
out of each of you.

20:06.171 --> 20:09.505
-Soldier: You can't talk
to us like that!
-Shut the fuck up!

20:09.588 --> 20:12.421
This is Tula.
This is our mine.

20:13.380 --> 20:15.505
We don't leave
unless we know why.

20:17.296 --> 20:18.672
Mm.

20:22.546 --> 20:24.630
You're going to Chernobyl.

20:26.672 --> 20:29.046
Do you know
what's happened there?

20:29.129 --> 20:31.380
We dig up coal, not bodies.

20:31.463 --> 20:34.630
The reactor fuel is going
to sink into the ground

20:34.713 --> 20:37.963
and poison the water
from Kiev to the Black Sea.

20:38.046 --> 20:39.505
All of it.

20:40.421 --> 20:42.004
Forever, they say.

20:43.922 --> 20:47.213
They want you to stop
that from happening.

20:47.296 --> 20:49.546
And how are
we supposed to do that?

20:50.963 --> 20:54.213
They didn't tell me,
because I don't need to know.

20:55.463 --> 20:58.213
Do you need to know,
or have you heard enough?

21:25.421 --> 21:26.838
(pats)

21:30.421 --> 21:33.088
(men muttering)

21:39.088 --> 21:42.088
Now you look like
the minister of coal.

21:55.296 --> 21:57.254
(labored breathing)

22:01.380 --> 22:03.463
(moans softly)

22:03.546 --> 22:05.046
Vasya?

22:06.546 --> 22:07.880
Vasya?

22:08.880 --> 22:11.463
(inhales sharply)

22:13.963 --> 22:15.880
(softly):
No, no, no.

22:15.963 --> 22:18.213
They told you no touching.

22:18.296 --> 22:20.546
It's not safe.

22:20.630 --> 22:22.922
They touch you.
(kisses)

22:23.963 --> 22:26.088
If it's safe for them,
it's safe for me.

22:28.838 --> 22:31.421
(breathing shakily)

22:36.088 --> 22:38.004
Where are the others?

22:38.088 --> 22:40.588
They took them
to a special room.

22:41.546 --> 22:43.296
They won't tell me where.

22:47.588 --> 22:50.046
Will you open the curtains?

22:50.129 --> 22:53.421
-Hmm?
-Open the curtains.

22:56.838 --> 22:58.505
Aah.

22:58.588 --> 23:00.672
(panting)

23:02.963 --> 23:04.380
(grunts softly)

23:09.963 --> 23:12.046
(laughing)

23:15.505 --> 23:18.421
Please, tell me
what you see outside.

23:18.505 --> 23:20.046
Tell me everything.

23:27.630 --> 23:28.963
Huh.

23:30.546 --> 23:32.630
I can see the Red Square.

23:35.380 --> 23:37.421
And...

23:37.505 --> 23:39.213
the Kremlin.

23:40.463 --> 23:43.922
Spasskaya Tower,
the Mausoleum.

23:46.296 --> 23:48.797
You see St. Basil's?

23:48.880 --> 23:51.004
Yeah.

23:51.088 --> 23:52.963
Ah.

23:53.046 --> 23:54.838
Yes, it's beautiful.

23:56.463 --> 23:58.254
I told you.

23:58.338 --> 24:01.672
I told you I'd show
you Moscow, remember?

24:01.755 --> 24:04.713
-Huh?
-Yeah. Yes.

24:10.505 --> 24:12.338
Thank you.

24:16.129 --> 24:18.922
(softly panting)

24:30.129 --> 24:32.213
(man groans)

24:35.296 --> 24:36.880
(man retches)

24:48.755 --> 24:51.129
(labored breathing)

24:59.463 --> 25:02.296
I'm not eating that.
It's shit.

25:03.046 --> 25:05.296
Get me something else.

25:05.380 --> 25:08.129
I'm not a nurse,
Comrade Dyatlov.

25:08.213 --> 25:10.171
I'm a nuclear physicist.

25:10.880 --> 25:13.505
Well, then, Comrade
Nuclear Physicist...

25:14.797 --> 25:19.254
unless you happen to have
a butter and caviar sandwich
on you,

25:19.338 --> 25:22.588
you can get the fuck
out of my room.

26:40.338 --> 26:41.672
What?

26:43.171 --> 26:45.672
I'm not good at this, Boris.

26:45.755 --> 26:47.505
The lying.

26:51.963 --> 26:54.880
Have you ever spent
time with miners?

26:56.546 --> 26:57.838
No.

26:57.922 --> 27:00.463
My advice: tell the truth.

27:00.546 --> 27:04.171
These men work in the dark.
They see everything.

27:05.546 --> 27:08.046
Andrei Glukhov, crew chief.

27:23.463 --> 27:25.380
Do these work?

27:26.296 --> 27:28.088
To an extent.

27:30.755 --> 27:32.755
Of course.

27:44.380 --> 27:46.713
So what's the job?

27:47.922 --> 27:51.505
We need to install a liquid
nitrogen heat exchanger

27:51.588 --> 27:54.713
underneath this concrete pad.

27:54.797 --> 27:58.713
There's no way to approach
from the interior
of the building,

27:58.797 --> 28:00.838
so you have to get at it
from underground.

28:00.922 --> 28:04.713
-And what's above the pad?
-The core of
the nuclear reactor,

28:04.797 --> 28:07.755
which is melting down.

28:07.838 --> 28:10.421
What? Like...

28:11.963 --> 28:13.171
Essentially.

28:15.004 --> 28:16.338
Is it gonna fall
on top of us?

28:16.421 --> 28:18.421
Not if you're done
within six weeks.

28:20.380 --> 28:22.254
Dimensions?

28:25.254 --> 28:27.171
Break ground here,

28:27.254 --> 28:29.546
dig a tunnel
150 meters to here,

28:29.630 --> 28:32.755
excavate a space
30 by 30 meters

28:32.838 --> 28:34.463
for the heat exchanger.

28:34.546 --> 28:37.713
And because we need to keep
disruption of the ground above
to a minimum,

28:37.797 --> 28:39.672
you can't use
any heavy machinery.

28:39.755 --> 28:41.129
It has to be done by hand.

28:41.213 --> 28:43.505
Then I need more men.

28:45.046 --> 28:46.380
Four hundred at least.

28:46.463 --> 28:48.963
We'll have to work
around the clock.

28:49.046 --> 28:50.880
How deep do you want
this tunnel? Six meters?

28:50.963 --> 28:53.880
-Twelve.
-Twelve? Why?

28:53.963 --> 28:56.463
For your protection.

28:56.546 --> 29:00.380
At that depth,
you'll be shielded from
much of the radiation.

29:00.463 --> 29:04.713
The entrance to the tunnel
won't be 12 meters below ground.

29:06.004 --> 29:07.838
No.

29:07.922 --> 29:10.963
And we're not 12 meters
below ground now.

29:15.588 --> 29:18.546
No. We're not.

29:21.296 --> 29:23.296
Shcherbina:
We have some equipment
here on site.

29:23.380 --> 29:26.546
More will arrive
by midnight.

29:28.046 --> 29:29.546
You can start
in the morning.

29:29.630 --> 29:31.129
No. We start now.

29:31.213 --> 29:35.171
I don't want my men here
one more second than
they need to be.

29:37.004 --> 29:40.672
If these worked,
you'd be wearing them.

29:46.338 --> 29:48.171
(sighs)

29:50.588 --> 29:52.296
Are they all like that?

29:52.380 --> 29:54.755
They're all like that.

30:14.880 --> 30:16.963
(lantern rattling)

30:18.963 --> 30:21.046
(men grunting)

31:09.463 --> 31:11.630
(men shouting indistinctly)

31:18.922 --> 31:20.129
Miner:
Yes?

31:20.213 --> 31:22.797
-What's it up to?
-Uh, 50 degrees.

31:27.129 --> 31:28.380
Fuck!

31:32.672 --> 31:34.546
Glukhov:
Hey!

31:34.630 --> 31:36.004
Hey you!

31:45.380 --> 31:48.380
-We need fans.
-For what purpose?

31:48.463 --> 31:50.296
What do you mean,
"For what purpose?"

31:50.380 --> 31:52.088
To dig your fucking tunnel,
that's why.

31:52.171 --> 31:55.046
-Who's talking to you?
-Whoa, whoa. Comrades.

31:55.129 --> 31:57.505
It's 50 degrees down there.

31:57.588 --> 31:59.213
We can't breathe
without the masks,

31:59.296 --> 32:00.755
we can't breathe
with the masks.

32:00.838 --> 32:03.713
It's like a fucking oven.
We need ventilation.

32:03.797 --> 32:06.922
Fans will put dust in the air,
the dust will go in your lungs.

32:07.004 --> 32:09.672
I've been breathing dust
in my lungs for 20 years.

32:09.755 --> 32:12.380
Not this dust.
I'm sorry.

32:12.463 --> 32:15.672
For your own good,
no fans.

32:22.380 --> 32:24.505
(man gasping quietly)

32:33.338 --> 32:35.505
(labored breathing)

32:43.672 --> 32:45.797
My name is Ulana Khomyuk.

32:45.880 --> 32:49.380
I'm a nuclear physicist
with the Chernobyl Commission.

32:51.213 --> 32:53.338
I want you to tell me
everything that happened

32:53.421 --> 32:55.546
on the night of the accident.

32:56.546 --> 32:58.213
Is that all right?

33:00.963 --> 33:02.254
Yes.

33:04.380 --> 33:05.963
I want to tell.

33:07.046 --> 33:08.588
All right.

33:19.213 --> 33:21.129
(wheezing)

33:21.213 --> 33:24.046
Your official title was?

33:26.588 --> 33:31.338
My name is Leonid
Fedorovych Toptunov.

33:31.421 --> 33:37.588
I am the senior reactor
control chief engineer

33:37.672 --> 33:40.296
at Chernobyl Nuclear
Power Plant.

33:43.922 --> 33:46.296
Senior engineer?

33:48.254 --> 33:50.088
How old are you?

33:54.713 --> 33:56.838
(gasping):
I'm 25.

34:39.004 --> 34:41.129
(gurney rattling)

34:44.588 --> 34:46.463
Vasily (weakly):
Lyusya? Lyusya?

34:46.546 --> 34:48.963
Yes, I'm here,
I'm here. I'm...

34:58.421 --> 35:00.546
(labored breathing)

35:03.963 --> 35:06.046
Have you been here
this whole time?

35:06.129 --> 35:08.672
No one said
I should leave.

35:08.755 --> 35:10.088
I did.

35:10.171 --> 35:11.421
Thirty minutes, I said!

35:11.505 --> 35:15.004
Well, where have you been?
When he's in pain?

35:15.088 --> 35:16.338
When his sores
stick to his gown?

35:16.421 --> 35:18.046
When he soils himself
five times a night?

35:18.129 --> 35:19.922
I've been looking after him.
Where have you been?

35:20.004 --> 35:21.838
I've been In the north
and west wing,

35:21.922 --> 35:25.421
where there are dozens
of patients from Chernobyl
exactly like him.

35:25.505 --> 35:27.171
-It isn't safe for you here.
-He's my husband.

35:27.254 --> 35:28.296
Not anymore.

35:28.380 --> 35:30.254
He's something else now.
Do you understand?

35:30.338 --> 35:33.088
He's dangerous to you.

35:33.171 --> 35:35.713
He's burned.

35:35.797 --> 35:37.463
Go home.

35:38.254 --> 35:39.630
Please.

35:42.713 --> 35:45.588
It won't take much longer.
I, uh...

35:49.088 --> 35:52.046
I don't want him
to die alone.

35:54.254 --> 35:56.588
Stay on the other side
of the plastic.

35:58.171 --> 36:00.046
Or I'll have you
removed by security.

36:08.463 --> 36:11.713
-(door opens, closes)
-(labored breathing)

36:15.630 --> 36:17.755
(Vasily wheezing)

36:59.296 --> 37:01.463
-Lyusya?
-Yes, my love.

37:04.463 --> 37:07.213
Is it day?

37:07.296 --> 37:09.546
No, it's nighttime now.

37:13.505 --> 37:15.380
I think I had a dream,

37:15.463 --> 37:17.380
it's just gone.

37:19.046 --> 37:20.630
Vasya.

37:26.296 --> 37:28.296
We're going to have a baby.

37:29.546 --> 37:31.672
(labored breathing)

37:57.380 --> 38:00.546
(door opens, closes)

38:05.129 --> 38:06.505
The fire's out.

38:09.171 --> 38:10.755
It's out, Valera.

38:11.880 --> 38:14.505
The miners are making
incredible progress.

38:15.505 --> 38:18.713
They say the whole job
will be finished in four weeks.

38:20.421 --> 38:22.338
Four weeks.

38:22.421 --> 38:24.546
Can you believe that?

38:30.338 --> 38:32.546
I know the job isn't over.

38:34.088 --> 38:36.088
But it's the beginning
of the end.

38:38.713 --> 38:40.546
-(knocking)
-(door opens)

38:41.672 --> 38:44.546
I'm sorry to bother you,
Deputy Minister, but...

38:46.505 --> 38:47.880
it is the miners.

38:47.963 --> 38:51.380
-(metal striking dirt)
-(miners grunting, coughing)

39:17.880 --> 39:20.088
(indistinct shouting)

39:36.088 --> 39:37.338
What?

39:37.421 --> 39:40.004
You wouldn't give us fans,
it's too hot for clothes.

39:40.088 --> 39:43.129
So we're digging the old way.
This is how our fathers mined.

39:45.129 --> 39:46.922
We're still wearing
the fucking hats.

39:47.004 --> 39:48.797
What do you want?

39:51.797 --> 39:54.546
You're not as protected now.

39:54.630 --> 39:57.338
Are you telling me
it will make a difference?

40:02.588 --> 40:04.672
When this is over,

40:04.755 --> 40:06.672
will they be looked after?

40:10.171 --> 40:11.963
I don't know.

40:22.713 --> 40:24.505
You don't know.

40:39.380 --> 40:41.505
(labored breathing)

40:43.171 --> 40:48.254
So the power level jumped
from 200 to 400 megawatts?

40:48.338 --> 40:50.171
Yes.

40:51.088 --> 40:52.838
Very fast.

40:54.171 --> 40:57.713
Why didn't you initiate
an emergency shutdown?

40:57.797 --> 41:00.505
Why didn't you press
the AZ-5 button?

41:02.088 --> 41:03.380
We did.

41:03.463 --> 41:07.046
I reported the increase
to Akimov,

41:07.129 --> 41:09.213
and he pressed
the button.

41:10.213 --> 41:13.630
Leonid, that's...
that's not possible.

41:15.088 --> 41:16.880
He did.

41:16.963 --> 41:18.922
I s-swear.

41:19.004 --> 41:21.129
I saw him do it.

41:24.713 --> 41:26.963
And that's
when it exploded.

41:29.755 --> 41:31.213
What?

41:33.463 --> 41:35.213
(door opens)

41:38.963 --> 41:41.046
(cart rattling)

41:45.046 --> 41:46.254
Khomyuk:
Um...

41:47.380 --> 41:50.463
-Which room is Akimov?
-Twenty-seven.

41:57.588 --> 41:59.630
(crying)

42:05.254 --> 42:09.171
Akimov:
I pressed it...
before the explosion.

42:09.254 --> 42:10.963
Before.

42:13.088 --> 42:15.713
(weakly):
But why?

42:15.797 --> 42:17.838
Why would that happen?

42:19.296 --> 42:22.755
I shut it down.
I pressed AZ-5.

42:24.588 --> 42:26.421
(Khomyuk breathes shakily)

42:28.546 --> 42:30.505
Thank you, Comrade Akimov.

42:32.630 --> 42:35.254
(labored breathing)

42:35.338 --> 42:37.380
Akimov:
I did everything right.

42:38.838 --> 42:40.963
I did everything right.

42:42.171 --> 42:43.797
(Khomyuk sighs)

43:12.004 --> 43:13.546
(whispering):
Get out.

43:13.630 --> 43:15.171
Get out. Get out of here.

43:15.254 --> 43:17.588
Let me go! Let me go!

43:17.672 --> 43:20.213
Stop it! Stop it!

43:22.838 --> 43:25.463
You let her in that room?
Inside the plastic,
touching him?

43:25.546 --> 43:28.088
-Did you know she's pregnant?
-It's not true!

43:28.171 --> 43:31.880
-What have you done?
-What kind of place is this?
Where is her protection?

43:31.963 --> 43:34.922
-Do you have any idea
what you're dealing with?
-Of course I do.

43:35.004 --> 43:36.463
-Please, I do not--
-No.

43:36.546 --> 43:38.755
-People are going
to hear about this.
-Wait.

43:38.838 --> 43:40.588
People are going to hear.
Do you understand?

43:40.672 --> 43:42.588
Everyone is going to hear.

43:42.672 --> 43:44.713
Man:
What is everyone
gonna hear?

43:50.880 --> 43:52.755
I am with the official
Chernobyl Commission,

43:52.838 --> 43:54.963
and I've been authorized
by Valery Legasov.

43:55.046 --> 43:58.296
-You can check this.
My name is Ulana--
-We know who you are.

44:01.713 --> 44:04.630
What is everyone gonna hear?

44:24.588 --> 44:26.546
Shcherbina;
You have your notes?

44:26.630 --> 44:28.213
Yes.

44:30.463 --> 44:32.171
Khomyuk was arrested
last night.

44:32.254 --> 44:34.963
What? Why?

44:35.046 --> 44:36.505
I don't know.

44:37.672 --> 44:41.004
-Was it--?
-Of course it was.

44:42.421 --> 44:43.546
I'm working on it.

44:43.630 --> 44:46.463
-Boris--
-I'm working on it.

44:47.713 --> 44:49.838
What more do you
want from me?

44:49.922 --> 44:51.421
Fix your tie.

44:55.421 --> 44:56.797
(door opens)

44:57.922 --> 44:59.338
They'll see you now.

45:09.421 --> 45:13.004
After thousands of sorties,
our brave helicopter crews

45:13.088 --> 45:14.505
successfully
extinguished the fire.

45:14.588 --> 45:17.213
The miners are working
heroically to ensure

45:17.296 --> 45:19.421
that the fuel does not
reach the groundwater.

45:19.505 --> 45:21.672
And furthermore,
there is no longer

45:21.755 --> 45:23.296
a threat of
additional explosion.

45:23.380 --> 45:28.213
The Soviet people
have faced the challenge
and risen to the task,

45:28.296 --> 45:30.880
and they and everyone
in this room are to be
commended.

45:36.088 --> 45:38.713
Lastly, Professor Legasov
and I have been vigilant

45:38.797 --> 45:41.171
to protect the security
interests of the State.

45:41.254 --> 45:43.838
And since the unfortunate
release of information

45:43.922 --> 45:45.213
directly following
the accident,

45:45.296 --> 45:48.254
we believe that there
has been no further lapse.

45:48.338 --> 45:50.755
Comrade Charkov,

45:50.838 --> 45:54.797
we hope we have lived up
to the highest standards
of the KGB.

45:54.880 --> 45:55.922
You have.

45:56.004 --> 45:57.672
Shcherbina:
Thank you.

45:58.838 --> 46:02.213
Professor Legasov
will now speak about

46:02.296 --> 46:03.755
the work that remains.

46:05.880 --> 46:07.546
Thank you.

46:11.004 --> 46:13.922
Deputy Chairman Shcherbina
has given you the good news,

46:14.004 --> 46:15.922
and it is good.

46:16.004 --> 46:18.546
The immediate danger is over.

46:18.630 --> 46:21.755
Now, I'm afraid,
a long war must begin.

46:22.880 --> 46:25.630
There is an enormous amount
of radioactive debris

46:25.713 --> 46:27.838
and contamination
spread out across a zone

46:27.922 --> 46:30.380
of approximately
2600 square kilometers.

46:30.463 --> 46:35.838
This entire region must be
completely evacuated.

46:35.922 --> 46:40.046
We must go to every town,
every village to ensure this.

46:40.129 --> 46:45.963
And all animals still
surviving within the zone,

46:46.046 --> 46:48.672
whether domesticated or wild,

46:48.755 --> 46:53.004
must be presumed contaminated
and will have to be destroyed

46:53.088 --> 46:56.463
to prevent the spread
of radiation and disease.

46:56.546 --> 46:59.963
In the immediate area
surrounding Chernobyl,

47:00.046 --> 47:05.505
uh, every rock, every tree,
the very ground itself,

47:05.588 --> 47:09.463
has absorbed a dangerous
amount of radionuclides,

47:09.546 --> 47:12.546
which will be carried
by the wind and the rain
if left exposed.

47:12.630 --> 47:14.963
So we will have to raze
entire forests.

47:15.046 --> 47:17.129
We will have to rip up
the top layer of earth

47:17.213 --> 47:18.505
and bury it under itself,

47:18.588 --> 47:22.129
approximately,
100 square kilometers.

47:23.838 --> 47:27.171
Um, and finally,
we will need to construct

47:27.254 --> 47:32.213
a containment structure
around the power plant itself,

47:32.296 --> 47:35.838
which will, of course,
still be extremely...

47:38.505 --> 47:40.421
There will be deaths.

47:43.755 --> 47:45.546
What amount of time,

47:45.630 --> 47:47.254
and how many men
do you require?

47:47.338 --> 47:51.088
We expect this liquidation
effort to take three years

47:51.171 --> 47:53.505
and approximately 750,000 men,

47:53.588 --> 47:58.963
including a number of doctors
and structural engineers.

47:59.046 --> 48:01.505
How many deaths?

48:01.588 --> 48:03.546
Thousands.

48:03.630 --> 48:06.171
Perhaps tens of thousands.

48:13.588 --> 48:15.296
Gorbachev:
Begin at once.

48:17.546 --> 48:19.630
(men murmuring)

48:20.713 --> 48:23.296
-Legasov: Comrade Charkov.
-Shcherbina: Valery!

48:24.963 --> 48:26.296
Yes, Professor?

48:27.338 --> 48:30.213
My associate was
arrested last night.

48:30.296 --> 48:31.630
Oh?

48:32.630 --> 48:35.838
I mean no disrespect,
but I was wondering
if you could tell me why.

48:35.922 --> 48:38.213
I assure you, I don't know
who you're talking about.

48:38.296 --> 48:41.088
She was arrested
by the KGB.

48:41.171 --> 48:44.213
You are the first deputy
chairman of the KGB.

48:44.296 --> 48:45.755
I am.

48:45.838 --> 48:48.755
That's why I don't have
to bother with arresting
people anymore.

48:48.838 --> 48:51.254
But you are bothering
with having us followed.

48:52.588 --> 48:55.046
I think the deputy
chairman is busy.

48:55.129 --> 48:57.254
No, no. It's perfectly
understandable.

48:57.338 --> 49:01.254
Comrade, I know you've heard
the stories about us.

49:01.338 --> 49:03.672
When I hear them,
even I am shocked.

49:03.755 --> 49:05.672
But we are not
what people say.

49:05.755 --> 49:08.505
Yes, people are
following you.

49:08.588 --> 49:11.004
People are following
those people.

49:11.088 --> 49:12.338
You see them?

49:14.755 --> 49:16.463
They follow me.

49:16.546 --> 49:20.630
The KGB is a circle
of accountability.

49:20.713 --> 49:21.922
Nothing more.

49:22.004 --> 49:24.421
You know the work
we're doing here.

49:25.797 --> 49:28.546
-You really don't trust us?
-Of course I do.

49:28.630 --> 49:31.838
But you know
the old Russian proverb:

49:31.922 --> 49:33.963
"Trust but verify."

49:35.880 --> 49:39.463
And the Americans think that
Ronald Reagan thought that up.

49:39.546 --> 49:40.880
Can you imagine?

49:42.004 --> 49:44.463
It was very nice
speaking with you.

49:44.546 --> 49:46.129
I need her.

49:48.713 --> 49:51.296
So you will be
accountable for her?

49:55.880 --> 49:57.421
Then it's done.

49:58.254 --> 50:01.296
-Her name is--
-I know who she is.

50:01.380 --> 50:03.213
Good day, Professor.

50:12.922 --> 50:16.505
No, that went
surprisingly well.

50:16.588 --> 50:18.755
You came off like
a naive idiot.

50:20.129 --> 50:22.922
And naive idiots
are not a threat.

50:38.421 --> 50:41.088
Man:
I'll come back when
the paperwork is complete.

50:48.755 --> 50:51.672
-Are you all right?
-They didn't hurt me.

50:53.463 --> 50:55.963
They let a pregnant woman
into a room with a...

50:56.046 --> 50:59.213
(sighs)
It doesn't matter.

50:59.296 --> 51:01.963
They were stupid.
I was stupid.

51:03.380 --> 51:05.380
Dyatlov won't talk to me.

51:06.588 --> 51:10.171
Akimov, yes,
Toptunov, yes, but...

51:10.254 --> 51:12.880
(sighs)
Valery,

51:12.963 --> 51:14.463
Akimov...

51:15.672 --> 51:17.380
his face was gone.

51:20.129 --> 51:21.797
You want to stop?

51:23.672 --> 51:26.129
Is that a choice I even have?

51:33.963 --> 51:37.755
Do you think the fuel will
actually melt through
the concrete pad?

51:37.838 --> 51:41.338
I don't know.
A 40% chance maybe.

51:43.838 --> 51:46.630
I said 50.
(chuckles)

51:46.713 --> 51:49.004
Either way, the numbers
mean the same thing:

51:49.088 --> 51:51.129
"Maybe."

51:51.213 --> 51:52.922
(sighing)

51:53.004 --> 51:56.296
Maybe the core will melt
through to the groundwater.

51:56.380 --> 51:58.755
Maybe the miners who I've told
to dig under the reactor

51:58.838 --> 52:01.254
will save millions of lives.

52:02.505 --> 52:05.004
Maybe I'm killing them
for nothing.

52:08.838 --> 52:10.880
I don't want to do
this anymore.

52:12.421 --> 52:13.922
I want to stop.

52:15.630 --> 52:17.129
But I can't.

52:18.296 --> 52:21.380
I don't think you have
a choice any more than I do.

52:22.755 --> 52:26.129
I think,
despite the stupidity,

52:26.213 --> 52:28.963
the lies, even this...

52:29.046 --> 52:31.129
you are compelled.

52:31.213 --> 52:33.630
The problem has been assigned,
and you will stop at nothing

52:33.713 --> 52:35.129
until you find an answer.

52:35.213 --> 52:38.380
Because that is
who you are.

52:40.213 --> 52:42.088
A lunatic, then.

52:43.922 --> 52:46.171
A scientist.

52:46.254 --> 52:48.129
(door unlocking)

53:07.129 --> 53:10.088
Did you know that they were
running a safety test?

53:11.296 --> 53:14.088
-Yeah.
-There's something else.

53:15.421 --> 53:18.588
Akimov says
they shut the reactor down,

53:18.672 --> 53:21.004
and Toptunov confirms it.

53:21.088 --> 53:24.922
-They pressed AZ-5.
-Apparently not soon enough.

53:25.004 --> 53:26.546
No.

53:26.630 --> 53:31.254
They say Akimov
pressed AZ-5,

53:31.338 --> 53:33.963
and then
the reactor exploded.

53:35.421 --> 53:38.296
If it had been just one of them,
I would have put it under

53:38.380 --> 53:40.630
faulty memory
or delusion even,

53:40.713 --> 53:44.505
but they both agreed.
They were adamant.

53:49.004 --> 53:50.505
Comrade?

53:52.630 --> 53:56.213
-Do you think it's possible?
-I think it makes no sense.

53:56.296 --> 53:59.755
I think it's what
I would say if I was trying
to cover my own mistakes.

53:59.838 --> 54:01.463
But?

54:02.588 --> 54:04.296
I believed them.

54:06.421 --> 54:07.880
Then you should pursue it.

54:07.963 --> 54:11.963
We have to pursue
every possibility,

54:12.046 --> 54:14.630
no matter how unlikely,

54:14.713 --> 54:17.672
no matter what
or who's to blame.

54:19.171 --> 54:23.505
I'll go back to the hospital
and reinterview Akimov
and Toptunov.

54:26.129 --> 54:27.755
If they're still awake.

54:29.129 --> 54:30.713
They're not.

54:32.505 --> 54:33.922
Guard:
Khomyuk.

55:28.588 --> 55:31.630
(soldier speaking indistinctly)

55:36.421 --> 55:38.713
(speaks indistinctly)

57:23.129 --> 57:25.171
(truck rumbling)

58:54.338 --> 58:56.797
(dosimeter clicking)

01:01:38.421 --> 01:01:40.505
♪ (FOLK MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

01:01:56.588 --> 01:01:58.505
ULYANA KHOMYUK:
To hell with our lives.

01:02:00.171 --> 01:02:02.129
Someone has to start
telling the truth.

01:02:03.171 --> 01:02:04.630
ANATOLY DYATLOV:
You think the right question

01:02:04.713 --> 01:02:05.797
will get you the truth?

01:02:06.672 --> 01:02:08.046
I know they're listening.

01:02:08.630 --> 01:02:10.171
There is no truth.

01:02:10.880 --> 01:02:12.171
(WOMAN YELPS)

01:02:12.588 --> 01:02:15.213
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪
